Consider the following multi-threaded code segment (in a mix of C and pseudo-code),
invoked by two processes P1 and P2, and each of the processes spawns two threads T1 and T2:

```c
int x = 0; // global
Lock L1; // global
main() {
    create a thread to execute foo(); // Thread T1
    create a thread to execute foo(); // Thread T2
    wait for the two threads to finish execution;
    print (x);
}
foo() {
    int y = 0;
